---
/* Problem Section */
---

<section id="problem" class="py-24 md:py-32 bg-core-background relative">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mb-20 reveal">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-ember mb-4">
                The problem
            </p>
            <h2 class="font-heading text-4xl md:text-5xl text-core-text-primary leading-[1.15]">
                Every morning, you're <span class="text-core-text-disabled line-through decoration-brand-ember/30">starting from zero.</span>
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-core-text-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
                You open Notion, check your backlog, scroll through half-finished docs — and still don't know what to actually build today. The problem isn't motivation. It's that nobody's given you a clear next step.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
            <!-- Card 1 -->
            <div class="reveal delay-1 group relative p-8 rounded-3xl bg-core-surface border border-semantic-border/30 hover:border-brand-ember/30 hover:shadow-card transition-all duration-300">
                <span class="absolute top-8 right-8 font-heading text-6xl text-core-text-disabled/10 leading-none select-none">01</span>
                <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-brand-ember-mist flex items-center justify-center mb-6 group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-ember" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2a3 3 0 0 0-3 3v7a3 3 0 0 0 6 0V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3Z"/><path d="M19 10v1a7 7 0 0 1-14 0v-1"/><line x1="12" x2="12" y1="19" y2="22"/><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><path d="m21 21-4.3-4.3"/></svg>
                </div>
                <h4 class="font-heading text-xl text-core-text-primary mb-3">No system connects your ideas to today</h4>
                <p class="text-core-text-secondary leading-relaxed text-[0.95rem]">
                    Your best ideas hit while you're away from your desk, then disappear in the gap between capture and execution. By the time you've researched the stack, compared tutorials, and picked an approach, momentum is gone.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Card 2 -->
            <div class="reveal delay-2 group relative p-8 rounded-3xl bg-core-surface border border-semantic-border/30 hover:border-brand-flax/30 hover:shadow-card transition-all duration-300">
                <span class="absolute top-8 right-8 font-heading text-6xl text-core-text-disabled/10 leading-none select-none">02</span>
                <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-yellow-50 flex items-center justify-center mb-6 group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-flax" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M8 2v4"/><path d="M16 2v4"/><rect width="18" height="18" x="3" y="4" rx="2"/><path d="M3 10h18"/><path d="m9 16 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
                </div>
                <h4 class="font-heading text-xl text-core-text-primary mb-3">The "What Now?" Loop</h4>
                <p class="text-core-text-secondary leading-relaxed text-[0.95rem]">
                    Side projects stay in the backlog because they feel too big. You don't have time to break down a full-stack app into bite-sized tasks — so you never start.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
